cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RUHSAT-Bench: a 473-claim abstention benchmark over Turkish construction and occupational-safety regulation"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite the paper and this archive."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Çetinkaya"
    given-names: "Ali"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7747-6854"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Engineering, Faculty of Technology, Selçuk University, Konya, Türkiye"
    email: "ali.cetinkaya@selcuk.edu.tr"
version: "1.0.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - compliance checking
  - decision-support software qualification
  - abstention
  - selective prediction
  - large language models
  - building regulation
  - Turkish law
abstract: >-
  RUHSAT-Bench is a set of 473 true/false claims over six frozen Turkish
  regulatory documents, each asked under a condition permitting an explicit
  "not sure" and a condition forcing a binary verdict, so that abstention
  behaviour is measured rather than assumed. The archive contains the source
  documents with checksums, three parsed corpora, the claim set in three
  gold-label versions, blinded expert-audit workbooks including a negative
  second-pass result, the pre-registration and its eight annexes, every run
  record, the scoring and analysis code, and a number sheet mapping every
  figure in the paper to the script that produced it.
